WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.019 --> 00:00:13.540
is the story of the Darling family.

2
00:00:14.781 --> 00:00:20.925
It is also the story of Peter Pan, a boy who may or may not exist—depending on how

3
00:00:21.065 --> 00:00:21.546
old you are.

4
00:00:22.667 --> 00:00:28.030
The Darlings lived at Number 14, a house in London, England, near Kensington Gardens.

5
00:00:29.571 --> 00:00:31.457
At first, the family was just Mr.

6
00:00:31.497 --> 00:00:33.157
George Darling and his wife, Mrs.

7
00:00:33.197 --> 00:00:35.718
Darling. But then their children were born.

8
00:00:36.659 --> 00:00:39.720
Wendy came first, then John, and then Michael.

9
00:00:41.221 --> 00:00:43.241
Later, Nana came to live with them.

10
00:00:45.382 --> 00:00:49.324
She was the children's nanny and made sure they were all well-cared for.

11
00:00:50.284 --> 00:00:55.066
Nana was a large, no-nonsense Newfoundland dog, who slept on the nursery floor.

12
00:00:56.327 --> 00:00:59.048
Mr. Darling was a good father and an excellent provider.

13
00:00:59.804 --> 00:01:05.527
During the day, he worked in the city as a banker, encouraging people to spend money wisely.

14
00:01:06.328 --> 00:01:08.269
He liked to work with numbers at home too.

15
00:01:09.790 --> 00:01:12.471
Mr. Darling counted how much money the children cost him.

16
00:01:13.432 --> 00:01:15.953
How much would he have to spend on their milk and cookies?

17
00:01:17.014 --> 00:01:19.515
How much money would he spend on their shirts and coats?

18
00:01:20.976 --> 00:01:25.758
When the children caught the German measles or the mumps, he worried about the cost of medicine.

19
00:01:26.679 --> 00:01:27.419
But he and Mrs.

20
00:01:27.459 --> 00:01:30.986
Darling agreed that the children were worth every penny spent.

21
00:01:32.547 --> 00:01:36.170
Mrs. Darling was more concerned about her children’s minds than about money.

22
00:01:37.370 --> 00:01:41.173
She was a lovely lady with a sweet mouth and a romantic sense of the world.

23
00:01:42.094 --> 00:01:46.437
Her mind was like a puzzle with many boxes, each one inside the other.

24
00:01:48.438 --> 00:01:50.380
Mrs. Darling thought about deep things.

25
00:01:51.200 --> 00:01:53.302
She worried about how her children were growing up.

26
00:01:54.343 --> 00:02:00.634
She knew from her own experience that when a child reaches the age of two, childhood is beginning

27
00:02:00.674 --> 00:02:01.094
to end.

28
00:02:02.695 --> 00:02:04.156
As a young girl, Mrs.

29
00:02:04.196 --> 00:02:05.496
Darling had many suitors.

30
00:02:06.577 --> 00:02:07.877
All of them wanted to marry her.

31
00:02:09.018 --> 00:02:12.920
But George Darling, who was a young man at the time, asked her first.

32
00:02:14.040 --> 00:02:15.101
He was very smart.

33
00:02:16.081 --> 00:02:20.483
One day, while the other boys were walking to her house to propose, Mr.

34
00:02:20.503 --> 00:02:21.684
Darling took a taxi.

35
00:02:24.544 --> 00:02:26.665
He got there ahead of the others and won her love.

36
00:02:27.625 --> 00:02:31.047
She happily gave him all her kisses, except for one.

37
00:02:31.727 --> 00:02:33.688
This kiss was her little secret.

38
00:02:34.688 --> 00:02:38.090
She saved it in the right corner of her sweet mouth for a special occasion.

39
00:02:39.590 --> 00:02:40.070
When Mrs.

40
00:02:40.110 --> 00:02:42.872
Darling was busy, Nana took care of the children.

41
00:02:44.052 --> 00:02:45.073
Nana was a treasure.

42
00:02:46.353 --> 00:02:50.715
Every morning, she walked the children in single file to Miss Fulsom’s kindergarten school.

43
00:02:52.235 --> 00:02:55.397
When they were well-behaved, Nana walked quietly by their side.

44
00:02:56.457 --> 00:03:01.299
When they were naughty, she barked and pushed them back into line with her huge head.

45
00:03:02.740 --> 00:03:06.361
She always carried an umbrella in her mouth, just in case of rain.

46
00:03:07.742 --> 00:03:11.503
Mr. Darling hired Nana as a nanny because she was much cheaper than a person.

47
00:03:12.524 --> 00:03:18.606
Even though the neighbors might gossip about a dog working as a nanny, the idea made perfect sense

48
00:03:18.646 --> 00:03:19.046
to Mr.

49
00:03:19.066 --> 00:03:25.218
Darling. Before Nana picked up the children from school, she waited in the basement with the other nannies.

50
00:03:25.959 --> 00:03:31.944
They complained about having a dog among them, and the neighbors did talk, but the Darlings didn't care.

51
00:03:33.325 --> 00:03:37.128
Before bedtime, there was always much merriment at Number 14.

52
00:03:38.309 --> 00:03:41.252
The children were allowed to sing and dance before going to bed.

53
00:03:42.213 --> 00:03:43.674
Oh, the dances were such fun!

54
00:03:44.695 --> 00:03:46.537
Nana barked in time with the music.

55
00:03:47.438 --> 00:03:49.940
The other servant, Liza, danced too.

56
00:03:51.484 --> 00:03:54.708
Mr. Darling watched alone and apart on the sidelines.

57
00:03:55.789 --> 00:03:56.309
But Mrs.

58
00:03:56.349 --> 00:03:58.852
Darling joined the children and spun around wildly.

59
00:03:59.853 --> 00:04:04.237
And sometimes she even planted her secret kiss on the cheek of one of the children.

60
00:04:05.138 --> 00:04:10.684
Yes, the Darling family lived very happily together—until the coming of Peter Pan.
